# Goal: a high-level task command, e.g. "move the red mug to the table", given to
# mission_executive_node. Structured input rather than free-text NLP (see Phase 6).
# Modeled as an action so an operator/caller gets live progress via MissionStatus
# feedback and can cancel a mission in progress -- a service would block with no
# feedback and no way to abort.

string object_class
# Target object category to search for and detect, e.g. "red_mug". Matched against
# DetectedObject.class_label.

geometry_msgs/PoseStamped destination_pose
# Where to place the object, in the map frame.

---

bool success
# True only if the mission reached the COMPLETE state.

string final_state
# The terminal MissionStatus.state value (e.g. "COMPLETE" or "FAILED").

string message
# Human-readable summary of the outcome.

---

MissionStatus status
# Live status updates as the mission progresses; identical in shape to what's
# published on /mission_manager/status.
